{
  "slug": "spec-engine",
  "name": "Spec Engine",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Spec-driven development engine: turns feature specs into working code through structured requirements, wave-based parallel agent execution, and automated quality gates.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **19 skills** and **13 agents**.\n\n- **Skills** (19): `spec` (Start a new spec-driven development workflow for a feature), `spec-accept` (Run user acceptance testing against spec requirements), `spec-brainstorm` (Brainstorm a feature idea through conversation until it is ready for /spec), `spec-dashboard` (Show verified status of all specs in the current project), `spec-docs` (Generate user-facing documentation from spec and implementation), `spec-exec` (Execute one spec task iteration with quality gates), `spec-import` (Import a markdown document and convert it to spec requirements), `spec-loop` (Loop spec execution with wave-based batching until all tasks complete), and 11 more\n- **Agents** (13): `spec-acceptor` (Performs user acceptance testing), `spec-consultant` (Domain expert consultant for brainstorming sessions), `spec-debugger` (Fixes issues when quality gates fail, tester rejects, or reviewer rejects), `spec-documenter` (Generates user-facing documentation from spec files and implemented code), `spec-implementer` (Implements code for assigned tasks), `spec-planner` (Writes requirements.md and design.md for a new spec), `spec-reviewer` (Reviews code quality, security, and architectural alignment), `spec-security-auditor` (Executes the 15-phase CSO security audit methodology (phases 0-14)), and 5 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install spec-engine@claude-community` from `farshidghyasi/spec-engine`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
